guides=[
('whey-protein','Whey protein','Protein','Compare concentrate, isolate, and the label behind the scoop.','Compare protein grams per serving, ingredient lists, milk allergens, and total cost. Concentrate and isolate are different product formats; choose based on your dietary needs and the actual label, rather than premium branding.','Protein grams per serving|Milk allergen statement|Sweeteners and flavorings|Cost per serving','Compare the cost for the amount of protein you intend to buy. A smaller scoop can make a tub appear to contain more servings without providing better value.'),
('plant-protein','Plant protein','Protein','Find a plant-based powder that fits your preferences.','Start with the protein source: pea, soy, rice, or a blend. Check every ingredient if you avoid animal products; a plant-themed label does not substitute for reading the full formula.','Protein source|Allergen statement|Protein per serving|Texture and flavor','Buy a small size first if taste matters to your routine. A large discounted tub is poor value if you will not use it.'),
('creatine','Creatine monohydrate','Strength','A straightforward checklist for comparing creatine labels.','Compare clearly labeled creatine monohydrate products. A single-ingredient formula is easier to evaluate than a blend. This guide compares packaging and value; it does not prescribe a dose or guarantee results.','Named ingredient form|Amount per serving|Number of servings|Independent certification','Calculate cost per gram of the listed creatine ingredient. Do not compare scoop sizes when one scoop also contains flavorings or other ingredients.'),
('pre-workout','Pre-workout','Training','Read the whole formula before choosing a blend.','Compare disclosed ingredient quantities and caffeine information. A proprietary blend can make products difficult to compare because individual amounts may be unclear. More ingredients do not establish better performance.','Caffeine disclosure|Individual ingredient quantities|Serving size|Other stimulant ingredients','Compare the full serving, not the front-label claims. Check whether the directions define one serving as more than one scoop.'),
('stimulant-free','Stimulant-free pre-workout','Training','Compare formulas without relying on energy claims.','Read all ingredients rather than assuming that a stimulant-free marketing label answers every question. Ask the manufacturer about unclear ingredients. Evidence for a finished multi-ingredient product can differ from research on one component.','Full ingredient list|Disclosed amounts|Certification|Cost per serving','Pay for ingredients you can identify and evaluate. A long label is not evidence of greater value.'),
('electrolytes','Electrolyte mixes','Hydration','Compare what is actually in each packet.','Electrolyte mixes vary in sodium, other minerals, carbohydrates, and sweeteners. Compare the prepared serving using the recommended water volume; packet weight alone is not a useful comparison.','Sodium per serving|Sugar and carbohydrates|Mixing volume|Dietary restrictions','Compare cost per prepared serving and the package directions. Different formulas serve different preferences; this is not a universal recommendation to supplement.'),
('protein-bars','Protein bars','Protein','Read beyond the protein number on the wrapper.','Compare the entire nutrition label, ingredients, and allergens. Bar size varies, so compare both per bar and per equal weight when assessing value. A convenient snack is not automatically a complete meal.','Protein per bar|Calories and serving size|Allergens|Sweeteners and texture','Start with a single bar before buying a box. Flavor, texture, and your own tolerance determine whether the purchase is practical.'),
('budget-protein','Protein powder on a budget','Value','Use a consistent comparison instead of tub size.','Record the package price, number of servings, and protein per serving. Compare equivalent protein quantities across the products you are considering. Keep shipping and recurring subscription terms in the total.','Total delivered price|Protein quantity|Subscription conditions|Return policy','Divide the total price by total protein grams, then multiply by 25 to compare cost for 25 grams of protein. This is a shopping unit, not a suggested dose.'),
('third-party-testing','Third-party testing','Quality','Check certification claims at their source.','Look for the exact certification program, product, and variant. A brand-wide statement or a laboratory-looking graphic does not establish that every item is certified. Confirm claims in the certifier’s directory.','Exact product name|Certifier directory listing|Scope of testing|Lot details when available','Certification can help you evaluate a claim, but does not promise that a supplement works or is appropriate for you.'),
('beginner-checklist','Before buying your first supplement','Essentials','Start with a need, a label, and a realistic budget.','Identify why you are considering a supplement and what information would justify the purchase. Review food, training, and practical constraints first. Avoid buying a large stack simply because several products are marketed together.','Reason for purchase|Full label|Total monthly cost|Questions for a qualified clinician','Buy only what you can justify. Skip guarantees of rapid transformation and seek professional guidance for personal health decisions.')]
